<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="experiment-flags" data-rev="0">
  <!-- @include-skip the files-touched rows are grouped per module with collapsible cards, matching the sibling plan fragments -->
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/flags.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The flag entry (owner, hypothesis, removal condition, state, overrides), the code-flag registry (empty when this slice lands), the states parsed from name=on|off, and apply: the overrides of every flag that is on are written into the tuning file, and the whole file is validated again.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>crates/engine/src</td><td>+190</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/data/tuning.rs, data/mod.rs, lib.rs, sim.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">An optional flags block in the tuning file with no version change; a flag that switches nothing is refused; the effective states apply once at load; the list of flags that are on enters the content digest when a state differs from the file; the match configuration carries the list.</div></details></td><td>new + modified</td><td>crates/engine/src</td><td>+56 / -2</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">observability</span> crates/engine/src/observe/mod.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">Every statistics record names the flags that were on; the calibration report gains the declared flags and, on a paired run, both arms, one comparison row per suite and band, and a verdict.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine/src</td><td>+45</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">observability</span> crates/engine-cli/src/report/compare.rs; report/mod.rs (modified)</summary><div class="pl-card">Pure comparison: off and on values per band with the delta and both pass marks; the verdict rule (bands passed, then distance to the band centre with a 0.05 margin; the on arm is rejected on a dark path, a violation, or a single-thread time 10 percent slower); a side-by-side table.</div></details></td><td>new + modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli/src/report</td><td>+180 / -2</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">cli</span> crates/engine-cli/src/cli.rs, calibrate/mod.rs, calibrate/worker.rs, bench.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">--flag name=on|off pins a state; --pair name runs the off arm and the on arm on the same fixtures and seeds into two arm folders, measures each arm's single-thread figure, and writes one report. The exit code reports whether the run can be trusted, not which arm won.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli</td><td>+91 / -10</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/engine/tests/flags.rs, crates/engine-cli/tests/calibrate_pair.rs; content.rs (modified)</summary><div class="pl-card">Six refusal cases for a missing or empty owner, hypothesis, or removal condition, each naming the flag; refusals for a flag that switches nothing, an unknown override path, and an out-of-bound value; a paired run on a test flag whose report validates against the schema and holds both values in every row.</div></details></td><td>new + modified</td><td>tests</td><td>+372</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> schemas/observability/run-report.schema.json, match-stats.schema.json</summary><div class="pl-card">Additive optional keys at schema version 1: the pair, the arms, the comparison rows, the verdict, and the flags that were on.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>schemas/observability</td><td>+86</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">docs</span> content/tuning.json, content/README.md, docs/how-to/modding.md, docs/reference/cli.md, docs/reference/data-files.md, README.md</summary><div class="pl-card">An empty flags block in the shipped file; the field reference and refusal messages; the paired-run how-to with the removal checklist for the losing arm; the two new calibrate flags in the command-line reference.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>content/ and docs/</td><td>+112</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R1 · Flags outlive their experiment</div><div class="callout-body">Owner, hypothesis, and removal condition are required and non-empty; a flag must switch something; flags that are on are logged at load; the paired report repeats the removal condition; the how-to carries the removal checklist.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R2 · The calibration harness is planned, not built</div><div class="callout-body">Every harness name comes from the calibration plan. Step 1 reads the landed code and stops for a plan re-review if it differs.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R3 · An override escapes its bound</div><div class="callout-body">The patched file is validated again as a whole, and a test sets an out-of-bound override and expects a refusal that names the flag.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R4 · A paired run takes twice as long</div><div class="callout-body">The budget stays per 1000-match suite, the report carries each arm's times, and --suite narrows a paired run.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R5 · A result is not marked with its flags</div><div class="callout-body">The flags that are on enter the content digest when a state differs from the file, and every statistics record names them.</div></aside>
  </div>
  <details class="pl-revs"><summary>0 prior revisions</summary><ul></ul></details>
